From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-vayu: hold the PM8150L RF LDOs on (EXPERIMENT)

Experiment for tracker issue #6, not for upstream.

Reading the PMIC registers directly (SPMI regmap in debugfs) with the modem
running shows six PM8150L LDOs off: l1 (1.8 V), l4 (1.7 V), l6 (2.9 V),
l7 (3.0 V), l8 (1.8 V), l9 (2.9 V). l4/l5/l6 are vddpx (IO). l1/l7/l8/l9
carry no AP-side purpose on any sm8150 board in mainline - i.e. they are the
rails the reference design leaves to the modem - and their voltages are what
PAs (3 V) and tuner/switch logic (1.8 V) want. Watching their EN bits while
the radio comes up shows the modem never tries to turn them on before it
asserts in RFLM.

Hold the four on and see whether the silent RF devices in the scheduler
journal (log 0x1843) start answering. Voltages are the ones RPMh already
programmed (matches the vendor tree); only the enable state changes.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
@@ -408,6 +408,8 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			/* RF front end supply (experiment, see tracker #6) */
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vdda_wcss_adcdac_1:
@@ -457,18 +459,24 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2856000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3104000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			/* RF front end supply (experiment, see tracker #6) */
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l8c_1p8: ldo8 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			/* RF front end supply (experiment, see tracker #6) */
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l9c_2p9: ldo9 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2704000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <2960000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			/* RF front end supply (experiment, see tracker #6) */
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l10c_3p3: ldo10 {
